               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">All interior nodes in this specification can have a node named
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Ext</fo:inline>. These nodes are the <fo:inline font-style="italic">extension</fo:inline>
      nodes. If an implementation needs to expose additional details about an
      interior node then they should expose these extensions under the
      corresponding <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Ext</fo:inline> node. To reduce name conflicts, it is
      recommended to group together implementation specific extensions under a
      unique name, recommended is to use the reverse domain name. For example,
      the following DDF defines an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Ext</fo:inline> node with extensions for
      the ACME provider.</fo:block>
